        B.q("psm-p4-79", "psm-product-backlog", "The Developers keep a separate list of technical improvements that the Product Owner never sees, and plan to work through it in a hardening Sprint. What fits the Scrum Guide?", listOf("The Product Backlog is the single source of work for the Scrum Team, so this work belongs there, visible and ordered", "That is fine; technical work is the Developers' business only", "That is fine if the Scrum Master keeps the list", "A hardening Sprint is the right place for technical work"), setOf(0),
            "The Product Backlog is an emergent, ordered list of what is needed to improve the product and the single source of work undertaken by the Scrum Team. Hidden lists break transparency.",
            whyWrong = mapOf(
                1 to "How the work is done is the Developers' call, but which work is done comes from the one Product Backlog.",
                2 to "Who keeps a hidden list makes no difference; there is still a second source of work.",
                3 to "Hardening Sprints are not part of Scrum; they defer work that should be Done.",
            ),
        ),
        // Sprint Backlog
        B.q("psm-p4-80", "psm-sprint-backlog", "A team believes the Sprint Goal only matters at the Sprint Review; day to day, the Developers just work through their tasks. What does the Scrum Guide say?", listOf("Right; the Sprint Goal is checked only at the Review", "As the Developers work during the Sprint, they keep the Sprint Goal in mind", "The Sprint Goal is checked only by the Product Owner", "The Sprint Goal matters only at Sprint Planning"), setOf(1),
            "The Guide says that as the Developers work during the Sprint, they keep the Sprint Goal in mind. The Daily Scrum inspects progress toward it every working day.",
            whyWrong = mapOf(
                0 to "The Daily Scrum inspects progress toward the Sprint Goal daily, not only at the Review.",
                2 to "The Sprint Goal is the Developers' commitment; they keep it in mind as they work.",
                3 to "It is defined at Sprint Planning, then guides the work throughout the Sprint.",
            ),
        ),
        B.q("psm-p4-81", "psm-sprint-backlog", "A stakeholder believes the Sprint Goal is met only if every selected item is finished exactly as planned. What does the Scrum Guide say?", listOf("Right; the Sprint Goal is the list of selected items", "The Sprint Goal provides flexibility in terms of the exact work needed to achieve it", "The Sprint Goal is met if half the items are finished", "The Sprint Goal is optional"), setOf(1),
            "The Guide says the Sprint Goal is the single objective for the Sprint and provides flexibility in terms of the exact work needed to achieve it. The selected items serve the goal; they are not the goal.",
            whyWrong = mapOf(
                0 to "The Sprint Goal is a single objective, not a list of items.",
                2 to "There is no percentage rule; the goal is met when its objective is met.",
                3 to "Every Sprint has a Sprint Goal; it is the commitment for the Sprint Backlog.",
            ),
        ),
        B.q("psm-p4-82", "psm-sprint-backlog", "A company expects the Scrum Master to keep the Sprint Backlog up to date for the Developers. What does the Scrum Guide say?", listOf("Right; the Scrum Master maintains the Sprint Backlog", "The Product Owner maintains it", "The Sprint Backlog is a plan by and for the Developers, who update it throughout the Sprint", "It is updated only at the Daily Scrum, by whoever runs it"), setOf(2),
            "The Guide says the Sprint Backlog is a plan by and for the Developers, and is updated throughout the Sprint as more is learned. Keeping it current is part of their own planning.",
            whyWrong = mapOf(
                0 to "The Scrum Master may coach, but the Sprint Backlog is the Developers' own plan.",
                1 to "The Product Owner orders the Product Backlog; the Sprint Backlog belongs to the Developers.",
                3 to "It is updated throughout the Sprint, by the Developers, as they learn.",
            ),
        ),
        B.q("psm-p4-83", "psm-sprint-backlog", "This Sprint holds mostly unrelated bug fixes, so the Product Owner says a Sprint Goal is not needed this time. What fits the Scrum Guide?", listOf("Every Sprint has a Sprint Goal; it gives coherence and focus and encourages the team to work together rather than on separate initiatives", "That is fine for maintenance Sprints", "That is fine if the Developers agree", "The list of bug fixes is the Sprint Goal"), setOf(0),
            "The Sprint Goal is the single objective for the Sprint and the commitment for the Sprint Backlog. It creates coherence and focus, encouraging the Scrum Team to work together rather than on separate initiatives.",
            whyWrong = mapOf(
                1 to "The Guide has no maintenance Sprints without a goal.",
                2 to "Agreement does not remove a commitment the Guide attaches to every Sprint Backlog.",
                3 to "A list of items is the what; the Sprint Goal is a single objective that says why the Sprint is valuable.",
            ),
        ),
        B.q("psm-p4-84", "psm-sprint-backlog", "A team keeps only the selected items in its Sprint Backlog. The Sprint Goal is in an email, and the plan is in people's heads. What is missing from its Sprint Backlog?", listOf("Nothing; the selected items are the Sprint Backlog", "The Sprint Goal and an actionable plan for delivering the Increment", "The Definition of Done", "The Product Goal"), setOf(1),
            "The Guide says the Sprint Backlog is composed of the Sprint Goal (why), the selected Product Backlog items (what), and an actionable plan for delivering the Increment (how). This team has only the what.",
            whyWrong = mapOf(
                0 to "The items are only the what; the why and the how belong in the Sprint Backlog too.",
                2 to "The Definition of Done is the Increment's commitment, not part of the Sprint Backlog.",
                3 to "The Product Goal is in the Product Backlog.",
            ),
        ),
        // Increment
        B.q("psm-p4-85", "psm-increment", "A manager says an Increment only counts once it achieves the whole Product Goal. How should a Done Increment from this Sprint be seen?", listOf("As work in progress until the Product Goal is reached", "As a concrete step toward the Product Goal that already counts", "As counting only once released to all users", "As counting only at the end of a release"), setOf(1),
            "The Guide says an Increment is a concrete stepping stone toward the Product Goal. The Product Goal is reached over many Increments, each of which counts as soon as it meets the Definition of Done.",
            whyWrong = mapOf(
                0 to "The Product Goal is long term; the Increments are the steps toward it.",
                2 to "Release is a separate decision; work becomes an Increment when it meets the Definition of Done.",
                3 to "Increments are created every Sprint, often several in one Sprint.",
            ),
        ),
        B.q("psm-p4-86", "psm-increment", "A team wants to show unfinished items at the Sprint Review, clearly labelled \"in progress\", to be transparent. What does the Scrum Guide say?", listOf("That is fine as long as they are labelled", "If a Product Backlog item does not meet the Definition of Done, it cannot be released or even presented at the Sprint Review", "Unfinished items may be shown if the Product Owner agrees", "They should be shown as part of the Increment"), setOf(1),
            "The Guide says that if a Product Backlog item does not meet the Definition of Done, it cannot be released or even presented at the Sprint Review. It returns to the Product Backlog for future consideration.",
            whyWrong = mapOf(
                0 to "Labelling does not change the rule; only Done work is presented.",
                2 to "No one can waive the Definition of Done for the Review.",
                3 to "Work that does not meet the Definition of Done is not part of the Increment.",
            ),
        ),
        B.q("psm-p4-87", "psm-increment", "A team uses each item's acceptance criteria as its Definition of Done, so every item has a different idea of Done. What is the problem?", listOf("There is no problem; that is what the Definition of Done is", "The Definition of Done is one shared quality standard for the Increment, not a different list for each item", "The Definition of Done should be written by the Product Owner for each item", "The Definition of Done only applies to large items"), setOf(1),
            "The Guide describes the Definition of Done as a formal description of the state of the Increment when it meets the quality measures required for the product. Item-specific criteria can be useful, but they do not replace the shared standard.",
            whyWrong = mapOf(
                0 to "Acceptance criteria are not mentioned in the Guide; the Definition of Done is about the Increment as a whole.",
                2 to "When the organisation has none, the Scrum Team creates the Definition of Done, and it is not item by item.",
                3 to "The same Definition of Done applies to everything that becomes part of the Increment.",
            ),
        ),
        B.q("psm-p4-88", "psm-increment", "Once the Scrum Team has agreed its Definition of Done, it cannot change it until the Product Goal is met. Is this statement true?", listOf("True", "False"), setOf(1),
            "The Definition of Done is among the things the Scrum Team inspects at every Sprint Retrospective, so the team can adapt it as it learns.",
            whyWrong = mapOf(
                0 to "Fixing the definition would remove one of the things the Retrospective is there to inspect and improve.",
            ),
        ),
        B.q("psm-p4-89", "psm-increment", "A team says its Definition of Done is the Developers' internal checklist, so stakeholders do not need to see it. Should it be shared?", listOf("No; it is for the Developers only", "Yes: the Definition of Done exists to give everyone, stakeholders included, a shared understanding of what work was completed as part of the Increment", "Only with the Product Owner", "Only with the Scrum Master, who keeps it"), setOf(1),
            "The Guide says the Definition of Done creates transparency by providing everyone a shared understanding of what work was completed as part of the Increment. Keeping it private defeats that purpose.",
            whyWrong = mapOf(
                0 to "The Developers conform to it, but its purpose is a shared understanding for everyone.",
                2 to "The Guide says everyone, not only the Product Owner.",
                3 to "The Guide gives the Scrum Master no ownership of the Definition of Done.",
            ),
        ),
        B.q("psm-p4-90", "psm-increment", "Two Increments were released to users mid-Sprint. The team says there is no need to show them at the Sprint Review, since users already have them. What does the Scrum Guide say?", listOf("Right; only unreleased work is shown", "The sum of the Increments is presented at the Sprint Review, supporting empiricism", "Only the last Increment is presented", "Released Increments are reviewed at the Retrospective instead"), setOf(1),
            "The Guide says the sum of the Increments is presented at the Sprint Review, thus supporting empiricism. Delivering early does not remove the need to inspect the outcome.",
            whyWrong = mapOf(
                0 to "Releasing early is allowed, but the Review still inspects the sum of the Increments.",
                2 to "The Guide says the sum of the Increments, not only the latest.",
                3 to "The Retrospective is about how the team works; the Increments are inspected at the Sprint Review.",
            ),
